n in classrooms with our  teachers and our educators with our  building leaders and i trust them that  they're going to follow the protocols  and we're going to have school look  everybody is so excited around what  we're doing bringing our kids back up  and that should be the focus of our work  be left here our leaders are ready and  so are we and so are families  all right so the next question deals  with what is the policy if there's a  confirmed kova's case at a school we're  currently working um you know the the  with the southern nevada health district  i mean these are things that are in our  implementation guide our principles we  follow contact tracing our nurses are  phenomenal our administrators are doing  a great job and really making sure the  quarantine process that's why masks are  so important you know i urge this  community to follow the direction of the  governor and our health officials you  know get vaccinated  wear your mask follow instructions so we  are in school in our classroom with our  kids  all right so one concern dr jarr  repeatedly raised last year was the  number of students lost to suicides  which is 24. so what is ccsd doing to  curb those numbers  once we started seeing an uptake up in  the self-harm we instituted like i  mentioned today you know uh beacon alert  go guardian we put it together in the  video multi-leadership district team  every school has a team of  of wraparound support systems for our  kids we the board um you know also  adopted uh panorama the universal  screener for us to be able to see and  the data will show you know we've had  suicide protocols about 600 plus to  protect our kids that work is going to  continue um because  you know great point and great question  we don't know how how deep  the scars are that is also one of the  priorities that we have  the well-being of our kids and our staff  is of our priority  the beacon alert program that dr jarrah  was talking about there is actually a  computer progra